\section{The settings}\label{sec:settings}

\subsection{The row}

For a space in $N$ variables the storage is one row
\[
\begin{aligned}
&\bigl(d_1,\ d_2,\ d_3,\ \Pi,\ F,\ o\bigr),\qquad d_1,d_2\in\N^N,\quad d_3\in\N^{3\times N},\\
&\Pi\ \text{a name or rows},\quad F\ \text{a name or rows},\quad o\in\N^{|F|\times N}\ \text{or empty for the default},
\end{aligned}
\]
and in one variable $\Pi$ is every pattern with a positive length. The free operator of the synthesis LPIs (\code{lpi.var.deg}) and the sizing options of the slack (\code{lpi.ineq}: \code{dD}, \code{dw}, \code{wmin}) are unchanged; the slack is sized by \code{get\_lift\_degs} from its target and comes out as a row of the same vocabulary, $d_1=d_2=D+1$ with $D=D_{\min}+\code{dD}$, $d_3=w+1$ in every block, and $F$ with its offsets from the \code{psatz} option, \code{'auto'} in the tiers.

\subsection{A tier layout}

Entries are indexed by the number of variables of the space, the last entry serving every higher number, as \code{poscopvar} reads \code{lpi.pos} today when \code{DEG} is omitted. The light tier of Section~\ref{sec:tiers} reads
\begin{small}\begin{verbatim}
% Lengths of monomial vectors, 0 = absent; entry k for a space in k
% variables, the last entry for every higher k. Rows of len_sos: the
% evaluation, complete-moment and incomplete-moment blocks.
st.lpi.pos = struct( ...
   'len_inc',  {{2,       [0 0],         [0 0 0]}}, ...             % d1
   'len_com',  {{2,       [2 2],         [2 2 2]}}, ...             % d2
   'len_sos',  {{[2;2;2], [1 1;2 2;0 0], [1 1 1;2 2 2;0 0 0]}}, ... % d3
   'patterns', {{'all',   'uniform',     'uniform'}}, ...
   'terms',    {{'none',  'none',        'none'}}, ...              % F
   'offsets',  {{[],      [],            []}});                     % o
\end{verbatim}\end{small}
The names are provisional. A tier file then differs from another in these six fields and nothing else, and one tier is nested in another exactly when its lengths are entrywise no larger, its pattern set and term set contained, and its offsets no smaller; the heavy-against-light defect of the 2-D cap tables cannot arise.

\subsection{The reader}\label{sec:reader}

One routine turns a row into the arguments of \code{poscopvar}, and replaces the three branches of \code{exec\_tools\_sop} and the omitted-\code{DEG} rule of \code{poscopvar}. For a space in $N$ variables:
\begin{enumerate}\setlength\itemsep{0pt}
\item the basis operators are the patterns of $\Pi$ whose factors are all positive, as \code{include} rows in the codes $1$, $4$, $2$ of $\ba$, $\bb$, $\bc$;
\item basis operator $\alpha$ gets the degrees \code{mult}$_k=\ell_k(\alpha_k)-1$ ($0$ for $\ba$, the canonical multiplier form) and \code{int}$_k=d_{3,\alpha_k,k}-1$, one specification per basis operator;
\item $F$, a name expanded to its rows, is \code{psatz\_rows}, with \code{psatz\_rows\_offset} the per-direction offsets $o$, the default rule of \eqref{eq:d4} when $o$ is empty;
\item an $\R^q$ space gets the identity basis at \code{int} $0$;
\item \code{sep}, \code{exclude}, \code{joint} and \code{subset} are not set.
\end{enumerate}
The executives route the storage of every dimension through this routine. The stock 2-D block stays reachable as an explicit override, a \code{settings\_2d} field given by the caller, since the row cannot write it (Section~\ref{sec:cannot}); the parked routing patch of 11/13/2026 is the 2-D branch of this change with the present \code{lpi.pos} in place of the row. The \code{'stock'} slack mode has its own fields and is untouched. Nothing in the operator classes, in \code{copquadvar} or in \code{poscopvar\_direct} changes except the parsing of a per-direction row offset.

